  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "rsyslog security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for rsyslog is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "RSYSLOG is the rocket-fast system for log processing.It offers high-performance, great security features and a modular design. While it started as a regular syslogd, rsyslog has evolved into a kind of swiss army knife of logging, being able to accept inputs from a wide variety of sources, transform them, and output to the results to diverse destinations.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nRsyslog is an open-source log processing system. The replace() function in the RainerScript scripting language has a heap buffer overflow vulnerability due to incorrect calculation of buffer size (CWE-131), leading to a heap-based buffer overflow (CWE-122). An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to cause denial of service or potential code execution.(CVE-2026-78002)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for rsyslog is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "rsyslog",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
